 # Claude Code — Hermes Orchestration Guide
 
 Delegate coding tasks to [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference) (Anthropic's autonomous coding agent CLI) via the Hermes terminal. Claude Code v2.x can read files, write code, run shell commands, spawn subagents, and manage git workflows autonomously.
 
+## When to Use
+
+Use this skill when the user needs Claude Code orchestrated through Hermes:
+- Delegating a coding task (bug fix, feature, refactor) to Claude Code
+- Running Claude Code in print mode for one-shot analysis or code generation
+- Setting up interactive tmux-based Claude Code sessions for multi-turn work
+- Orchestrating parallel Claude Code instances across worktrees
+- Reviewing PRs with Claude Code's diff analysis capabilities
+- Configuring Claude Code permissions, MCP servers, or settings
+- Debugging Claude Code session issues (dialog handling, context windows)
+- Managing Claude Code authentication, model selection, or cost controls
+
+## Not For
+
+- General Anthropic/Claude API usage → use `hermes-agent` skill or direct API calls instead
+- Delegating tasks to other AI coding agents → use `codex` for OpenAI Codex, `opencode` for OpenCode instead
+- Local LLM inference → use `llama-cpp` or `serving-llms-vllm` instead
+- Simple one-shot LLM queries → use direct terminal calls to `claude -p` without this skill's orchestration patterns
+- Hermes Agent configuration → use `hermes-agent` skill instead
+- MCP server management outside Claude Code → use `native-mcp` or `mcporter` instead
+
 ## Prerequisites
 
 - **Install:** `npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code`
